        <body>
            <div xml:id="d338">

                <pb facs="0686" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg648"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/6823: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-20T15:00:00-04:00">September 20, 1919—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3180. For Polk from Phillips. Your 4126, September 9, 7 p.m. and 4216, September
                    15, 3 p.m. were forwarded to the President and I have today received the
                    following reply: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Polk is taking exactly the right position with regard to the
                            continuation of the Conference and I hope you will give him our strong
                            support in the matter. It would be very nearly fatal to the whole state
                            of mind of the world, if the British were to withdraw and break up the
                            Conference.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I have not considered it necessary to forward your 4244, September 17, 7 p.m., as
                    the matter seemed sufficiently clear without the information contained in that
                    telegram.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
